// FICR — Factory Information Configuration Registers, nRF52840.
//
// Renode's stock nrf52840.repl does not model FICR, so the firmware reads zeros
// from 0x10000000 and later dereferences something derived from them, landing on
// 0xA5A5A5A5 (the uninitialised-memory fill). That was the boot failure.
//
// Modelled as read-only memory rather than a peripheral: FICR is factory-written
// and never changes at runtime, so a backing region with the right values is
// behaviourally exact and far simpler than a register model.
ficr: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x10000000
    size: 0x1000
